flowchart TD
    A([Requisition Submitted]) --> B[Budget Availability Check]
    B --> C{Budget Available?}
    C -->|No| D[Request Budget Exception]
    D --> E[Budget Committee Review]
    E --> F{Committee Approves?}
    F -->|No| G([Requisition Rejected])
    F -->|Yes| H[Vendor Selection & Sourcing]
    C -->|Yes| H
    H --> I{Preferred Vendor Exists?}
    I -->|Yes| J[Direct Award]
    I -->|No| K[RFQ Process]
    K --> L[Compare Vendor Quotes]
    L --> M[Purchase Order Created & Approved]
    J --> M
    M --> N{PO Value Above $50,000?}
    N -->|Yes| O[VP Additional Approval]
    N -->|No| P[Goods or Services Received]
    O --> P
    P --> Q[Vendor Invoice Received]
    Q --> R[Three-Way Match PO / Receipt / Invoice]
    R --> S{Match Successful?}
    S -->|No| T[Discrepancy Investigation]
    T --> U[Corrected Invoice Received]
    U -.->|Re-match| R
    %% [1] start
    S -->|Yes| V2[Payment Approval Requested]

    subgraph APMGR["AP Manager"]
        direction TB
        V[Payment Reviewed, Approved & Released]
    end

    V2 --> V
    %% [1] end
    %% [2] start
    V --> X{Payment Above $10,000?}

    subgraph FINDIR["Finance Director"]
        direction TB
        Y[Independent Payment Approval]
    end

    X -->|Yes| Y
    Y --> W([Payment Confirmation Sent to Vendor])
    X -->|No| W
    %% [2] end

    %% ⚡ CHANGED SECTION — Added audit logging records for AP Manager and Finance Director approvals
    LOG1>"Approval Log: Approver Name & Timestamp"]
    V -.- LOG1
    LOG2>"Approval Log: Approver Name & Timestamp"]
    Y -.- LOG2

    classDef dataObject fill:#fff9db,stroke:#d4b106,stroke-width:1px;
    class LOG1,LOG2 dataObject;
    %% END CHANGED SECTION

%% ═══ CHANGE LOG ═══
%% [1] AP Manager approval step — Added a "Payment Approval Requested" step and AP Manager subgraph so payment release is separated from the AP clerk's match duties.
%% [2] Finance Director second approval — Added a decision on payment amount above $10,000 that routes to a new Finance Director subgraph for independent approval before payment confirmation, otherwise proceeding directly.
%% [3] Approval audit logging — Attached data-object nodes to the AP Manager and Finance Director approval tasks capturing approver name and timestamp for audit evidence, without altering the main flow.

%% EXPLANATION:
%% Added two data-object nodes ("Approval Log: Approver Name & Timestamp") attached via dotted association lines to the AP Manager's "Payment Reviewed, Approved & Released" task and the Finance Director's "Independent Payment Approval" task. These artifacts record audit evidence without being inserted into the main sequence flow, consistent with BPMN data-object conventions. A shared `dataObject` classDef styles both log nodes.